body: "## Hosted failure and reproduction\nPR 1279 head 7674714d2 passed all 9060 hosted tests and exact coverage, plus the hosted import and transport cost gates. Its native shell smoke failed before assertions could run because Fish 3.7 rejected the stdin transport used by Node 24.20. The final validation comment also named the historical-evidence owner without a graph edge.\n\n## Fix and executable evidence\nPass the generated Fish program through explicit command mode (-c), keeping the source, hostile input cases, exit-status checks, stderr checks and literal-preservation assertions unchanged. A read-only Ubuntu 24.04 container with Node 24.20.0 and Fish 3.7.0 reproduces the original exit 127 and passes all 31 Fish/Zsh cases after the change. Native Fish 4.9.3 also passes all 31 cases.\n\nThe completion parent now verifies the historical-evidence owner, matching its actual validation comment. Graph composition passes all ten assertions and restores prose-edge gaps to 1236, exactly the existing ceiling. No graph budget, coverage exclusion, timing bound or test assertion changes.\n\n## Delivery boundary\nThis item owns only the hosted acceptance transport and graph receipt follow-up. Production SDK shell escaping remains the completed parent change. All final-head hosted checks remain mandatory before merging PR 1279."
